Z||000003||artherd||12-16-2001||09:08 PM||||Hi Tom, those would look niiice on your car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (even though they're fake '2-piece' just like my 17s in the sig!  Oh no!!! I've forgiven them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>One downside, they only come in 17x7 and 18x7.5 widths.    <P>You could do 17x7 front with 215/45/17 <BR>tyres, then in back go 18x7.5 with 245/40/18<P>Unfortunately they don't have for example a 17x8 wheel for the rear.<P>1FST2M6 has a similar 17 front, and 18 rear setup on his car, and I rather like the look (and he seems to like the performance.)<P>Shod them with sticky expensive short-wearing rubber, and they'll tighten your car up even MORE!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
